1
00:05:45,882 --> 00:05:51,882
The clock is ticking for the human race…

2
00:11:31,764 --> 00:11:37,764
Abduction is a horror, science fiction, thriller
film directed by Ernie Barbarash.

3
00:17:17,647 --> 00:17:23,647
A man steps out of a park fountain in Ho Chi Minh City with no
recollection of who he is or where he came from.

4
00:23:03,529 --> 00:23:09,529
As he wanders through the city, piecing together clues to his past,
he is relentlessly pursued by mysterious figures.

5
00:28:49,411 --> 00:28:55,411
Quinn, played by Scott Adkins.

6
00:34:35,294 --> 00:34:41,294
Conner, played by Andy On Chi-Kit.

7
00:40:21,176 --> 00:40:27,176
Maya, played by Lily Ji.

8
00:46:07,058 --> 00:46:13,058
Dao, played by Aki Aleong.

9
00:51:52,941 --> 00:51:58,941
Anna, played by Trương Ngọc Ánh.

10
00:57:38,823 --> 00:57:44,823
The Visitor, played by Daniel Whyte.

11
01:03:24,705 --> 01:03:30,705
Abduction is a 2011 American action thriller film directed by John Singleton (in his final directed film before
his death in 2019), produced by Roy Lee and Ellen Goldsmith-Vein, and written by Shawn Christensen.

12
01:09:10,588 --> 01:09:16,588
The film stars Taylor Lautner in the lead role, alongside Lily Collins, Alfred Molina,
Jason Isaacs, Maria Bello, and Sigourney Weaver in supporting roles.

13
01:14:56,470 --> 01:15:02,470
The film follows a young man who sets out to uncover the truth about his life
after finding his child photo on a missing-person's website.

14
01:20:42,352 --> 01:20:48,352
The film, Singleton's last before his death in 2019, was
released by Lionsgate on September 23, 2011.

15
01:26:28,235 --> 01:26:34,235
The film received negative reviews.

16
01:32:14,117 --> 01:32:20,117
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
